🚀 Top Terraform Best Practices with Real Examples 🧠
 When building secure and scalable infrastructure with Terraform, following structured patterns is crucial. Here's a guide I follow (and recommend) based on hands-on experience with AWS and multi-environment DevOps setups:

🔹 1. Use Modules to Keep Code Reusable & Organised
 Structure your Terraform like this:
module "vpc" {
 source = "./modules/vpc"
 vpc_config = var.vpc_config
}
✅ Reusable modules
✅ Better collaboration

🔹 2. Group Variables Using object Types for Clarity
 Instead of dozens of individual variables:
variable "vpc_config" {
 type = object({
 cidr_block = string
 subnets = list(string)
 })
}
✅ Logical structure
✅ Easy validation

🔹 3. Always Use Remote State with S3 & DynamoDB Locking
 In the backend.tf:
terraform {
 backend "s3" {
 bucket = "my-tf-state"
 key = "env/dev/terraform.tfstate"
 region = "us-east-1"
 dynamodb_table = "tf-locks"
 }
}
✅ Prevents state conflicts
✅ Enables team collaboration

🔹 4. Use Workspaces for Multi-Environment Deployments
 Create and switch:
terraform workspace new dev
terraform workspace select dev
✅ Avoids duplication
✅ Keeps states isolated

🔹 5. Manage Secrets Securely — Never Hardcode Them
 Use Secrets Manager:
data "aws_secretsmanager_secret_version" "db_pwd" {
 secret_id = "prod/db-password"
}

output "db_password" {
 value = data.aws_secretsmanager_secret_version.db_pwd.secret_string
 sensitive = true
}
✅ No plaintext secrets
✅ Role-based access control

🔹 6. Validate Variables to Catch Errors Early
variable "env" {
 type = string
 validation {
 condition = contains(["dev", "prod"], var.env)
 error_message = "env must be 'dev' or 'prod'"
 }
}
✅ Safe inputs
✅ Cleaner pipelines

🔹 7. Use locals for Common Tags and Logic
locals {
 common_tags = {
 Project = "MyApp"
 Environment = var.env
 }
}
✅ DRY principle
✅ Consistent tagging

🔹 8. Lock Provider Versions to Prevent Breakage
terraform {
 required_providers {
 aws = {
 source = "hashicorp/aws"
 version = "~> 5.30"
 }
 }
}
✅ Avoids unexpected changes
✅ Reproducible builds

🔹 9. Auto-Document with terraform-docs
 Run this:
terraform-docs markdown table ./modules/vpc > README.md
✅ Up-to-date docs
✅ Onboard new devs quickly

🔹 10. Scan Code Using tfsec or Checkov
 Run security scans:
tfsec .
# or
checkov -d .
✅ Detect misconfigs
✅ Enforce security best practices
